{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/54244-the-scroll-of-ages","id":54244,"title":"The Scroll of Ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-20T15:02:10-08:00","id":54244,"title":"The Scroll of Ages","content":"Are we ever going to actually see this feature, promised in the corebook, reveal itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T23:08:06-08:00","id":54499,"title":"","content":"I'd at least like to see this referenced in the Monday Meetings. It'd be nice to know that it hasn't been forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:14:18-08:00","id":55083,"title":"","content":"My brain does not seem to be working at the moment. What was the content of &quot;The Scroll of Ages&quot; supposed to be? <br /> <br /> I far as I remember the estimated release pattern for Mummy was:<br /> <br /> 1. Corebook<br /> 2. Guildhalls<br /> 3. Ready Made Characters<br /> 4. DC<br /> 5. Deceived<br /> 6. Sothic Ascendance<br /> 7. Rio<br /> 8. Dreams of Avarice/Mummy Anthology/Mummy novel <br /> <br /> As far as I am aware a few extra details are known. <br /> <br /> Firstly, the release pattern seems to have royally screwed up since the core books release. Guildhalls was about 6 months delayed and none of the future releases seem to be being developed particularly quickly especially when compared to the rate that Demon's or Strix content seems to be being developed. <br /> <br /> Secondly, Rio is almost certainly going to come out before Sothic Ascendance. As the latter has yet to even start development. <br /> <br /> Thirdly, we know that Dreams of Avarice was having a writer commissioned for hit (though personally I feel CAS should be writing it) back in late November/early December. So its possibly being written now, but is not on the Monday Morning notes at current. <br /> <br /> Fourthly, the Mummy Fiction Anthology is being written as of early December at least. How long it has been in that phase of development is unknown. <br /> <br /> Considering points three and four any of these three &quot;fluff&quot; books could be released at any time during the schedule.<br /> <br /> Fifth, there was talk of doing a &quot;Book of Going Westward&quot; after everything else if the sales for the Mummy line supported it. This got a descent amount of fan support as it was a possible Kickstarter goal that was missed by about 4K and was only placed as a reward in the last 12-24 hours of the Kickstarter. <br /> <br /> Sixth, in a developer interview CAS mentioned that there was going to be a book just about Apotheosis. He may actually be talking about Sothic Ascendance, but if not there seems to be at least one more &quot;hidden&quot; book not on the schedule at current.<br /> <br /> Some Mummy content will be in the new Hunter book &quot;Mortal Remains&quot;. <br /> <br /> Mummy will be getting an addition setting in Dark Era's this August that is from 1880-1920 (for anyone who wants to play &quot;pulp&quot; Mummy). <br /> <br /> Did not mean this post to be an info dump, but it seems to have become one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:28:12-08:00","id":55094,"title":"","content":"The Scroll of Ages<br /> All Storytelling games are about inspiration to<br /> one degree or another, but this is especially true of<br /> Mummy. The driving force behind a Storyteller\u2019s<br /> decision to run this game, as opposed to any other,<br /> is most often the desire to tell a particular story or<br /> explore a given idea through roleplaying. And that<br /> starts with inspiration.<br /> It\u2019s common in Storytelling games to include a<br /> list of references that are good for either inspiration<br /> or continuing education on the broader topic of the<br /> game. Given the wide variety of possible influences<br /> on a game this narratively dynamic (not to mention<br /> the fact that research references, if not the materials<br /> themselves, should be made free to the public<br /> whenever possible), we\u2019ve decided to put our list of<br /> inspirational sources for Mummy: The Curse and its<br /> associated topics online.<br /> Welcome to the Scroll of Ages\u2014our first interactive<br /> reference library. Here, you can come peruse not<br /> only our inspirational references, but those of other<br /> players, and if in your researching you stumble<br /> across something cool and appropriate, come<br /> on back and introduce it for future researchers.<br /> That\u2019s what the Scroll is all about. Site hosting is<br /> subject to change, but you can always come back<br /> to the game blog if you need a place to start:<br /> whitewolfblogs.com/mummy.<br /> <br /> Mummy the Curse, page 9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T04:49:25-08:00","id":55378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/54244-the-scroll-of-ages?p=55083#post55083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, Rio is almost certainly going to come out before Sothic Ascendance. As the latter has yet to even start development.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...Rio hasn't started writing or development either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Unless there's something I don't know. As of now, though, it seems that the novels/stories are in process of contracting commissions, and the DC Citybook and Book of the Deceived are in a sort of race to see who will finish first. It seems that, while the latter is behind schedule, we might get the Citybook according to its forecast release of March (or was it May?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T00:36:29-08:00","id":55996,"title":"","content":"Rich has referenced the Scroll of Ages in the latest Monday Meeting. Sothis Ascends has writers contracted and they are producing first drafts, but I can't speak for release dates of the sourcebooks mentioned above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:29:05-08:00","id":316563,"title":"","content":"Can we get an update on this, since it was actually promised in the beginning of the core book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","na